@startuml Sequence_Normal_Round
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam roundcorner 8

actor Client as "Client Node"
participant Gateway as "FastAPI Gateway\n(behind Caddy, HTTPS)"
database DB as "PostgreSQL"
database Storage as "File Storage (/data/models/)"
participant Coordinator as "Coordinator\n(separate process)"
participant Observability as "Reports & Observability"

note over Gateway, Coordinator
  The gateway and the coordinator never call each other;
  they communicate only through PostgreSQL and file storage.
end note

' ==============================================================================
' PRE-PHASE: ONBOARDING & CONFORMANCE
' ==============================================================================
== Pre-Phase: Onboarding & Conformance (details: 01_registration_conformance) ==
Client -> Gateway : POST /register + Bearer token
Gateway -> DB : Check token, approved list and client version
Gateway --> Client : 200 OK
Client -> Gateway : POST /conformance/report (including outputs on reference inputs)
Gateway -> DB : Re-check report and store the result
Gateway --> Client : 200 OK (conformant) / 422 (mismatch, with reason)

' ==============================================================================
' PHASE 0: OPEN THE ROUND
' ==============================================================================
== Phase 0: Open the Round (OPEN) ==
Coordinator -> Storage : global_model_v(t).safetensors (+ SHA-256)
Coordinator -> DB : Select a random subset of conformant, available clients (seeded)
Coordinator -> DB : Round t = OPEN → COLLECTING; store deadline and selected clients

' ==============================================================================
' PHASE 1: DISTRIBUTE THE MODEL TO CLIENTS
' ==============================================================================
== Phase 1: Distribute the Model (Task Polling & Model Download) ==
loop Task polling at a configurable interval
    Client -> Gateway : GET /task (client_id)
    Gateway -> DB : Active round? Is this client selected?
    alt Client not selected / no active round
        Gateway --> Client : 204 No Content (no task)
    else Client selected
        Gateway --> Client : TaskAssignment (run_id, round_id=t, model_version=t, deadline, config)
    end
end

Client -> Gateway : GET /model/{run_id}/{version=t}
Gateway -> Storage : Read global_model_v(t).safetensors
Gateway --> Client : Model file + SHA-256
Client -> Client : Verify SHA-256

' ==============================================================================
' PHASE 2: CLIENT-SIDE TRAINING
' ==============================================================================
== Phase 2: Client-Side Training (Local PyTorch Training) ==
Note over Client
  The client trains on its local data (raw data never leaves the client):
  • Evaluate global model v_t on the local test split (federated evaluation)
  • Local epochs and learning rate come from the round config
  • FedAvg: plain local training / FedProx: proximal term (μ) added to the loss
  • Compute local metrics again after training
  • Package updated weights as safetensors and compute SHA-256
  • Generate a new update_id (UUIDv4)
End Note

' ==============================================================================
' PHASE 3: UPLOAD UPDATES TO THE SERVER
' ==============================================================================
== Phase 3: Upload Updates (Update Upload & Validation) ==
Client -> Gateway : POST /update (run_id, round_id, update_id, model_version,\nnum_samples, metrics, weights, sha256)
Gateway -> Gateway : Verify token and SHA-256
Gateway -> DB : Stale / duplicate check (UNIQUE run_id, round_id, client_id)

alt Same update_id already accepted (retry after a lost response)
    Gateway --> Client : 200 OK (UpdateAck, idempotent)
else Another update_id already stored for this round (duplicate)
    Gateway --> Client : 409 Conflict
else Round closed, deadline passed or old model version (stale)
    Gateway --> Client : 409 Conflict (stale)
else Valid update
    Gateway -> Storage : Save client_{client_id}_v(t).safetensors
    Gateway -> DB : Store update record, transfer size/duration and client metrics
    Gateway --> Client : 200 OK (UpdateAck accepted=true)
end

note over Client, Gateway
  On network errors the client retries with exponential
  backoff + jitter, reusing the same update_id.
end note

' ==============================================================================
' PHASE 4: AGGREGATE THE WEIGHTS
' ==============================================================================
== Phase 4: Aggregation ==
loop Coordinator checks the database periodically
    Coordinator -> DB : Number of accepted updates for round t
end

alt All selected clients reported OR (deadline reached AND received >= min_participants)
    Coordinator -> DB : Round t = AGGREGATING
    Coordinator -> Storage : Read accepted client weights for this round
    Coordinator -> Coordinator : Sample-weighted average (FedAvg / FedProx)
    Coordinator -> Coordinator : Evaluate v(t+1) on the server-side held-out test set
    Coordinator -> Storage : Save global_model_v(t+1).safetensors
    Coordinator -> DB : Round t = DONE; round timings and metrics (for crash recovery)
else Deadline reached AND received < min_participants
    Coordinator -> DB : Round t = FAILED (reason stored); global model stays at v_t
end

alt More rounds to run
    Coordinator -> Coordinator : Open a new round (new round_id)
    Note over Coordinator, Client : The loop returns to Phase 0
else Configured number of rounds reached
    Coordinator -> DB : Run = COMPLETED
end

' ==============================================================================
' PHASE 5: DELIVER THE FINAL MODEL
' ==============================================================================
== Phase 5: Final Model Delivery (Final Model Artifact & ONNX) ==
Coordinator -> Storage : Export the final model to ONNX (final_model.onnx)
Coordinator -> Coordinator : Compare ONNX and PyTorch outputs on the reference inputs
Coordinator -> Storage : Save final_model.onnx + .safetensors + SHA-256
Coordinator -> DB : Store final artifact info (version, run_id, manifest version, checksum)

Client -> Gateway : GET /model/{run_id}/final + Bearer token
Gateway -> Storage : Read final model and checksum
Gateway --> Client : Final model + SHA-256
Client -> Client : Verify checksum and reproduce the reference predictions

Coordinator -> Observability : Trigger automatic reporting
Observability -> DB : Collect all round, event and system metrics
Observability -> Storage : Generate run_{id}_report.md, run_{id}_summary.json and CSV
Observability -> Storage : Plot ML and system metrics (.png)
note over Observability
  Grafana needs no update step:
  it reads metrics directly from PostgreSQL.
end note

@enduml
